# partial-concepts-name-collision sibling — a REAL library literally named "Pol Concepts"
library "Pol Concepts".

// `Sibling Concept` is a STANDALONE patient-age determination (a `source representation` over
// `Patient.birthDate`, no local `code is`). An age posrep lowers to an intrinsically-total
// boolean, so it clears the boundary-totality gate. Root's `From Sibling` aliases it
// cross-library, which forces the `include PolConcepts` on the Inferred layer this fixture asserts.
concept "Sibling Concept":
- value type is boolean.
- source representation:
  - type is Patient.
  - value element is Patient.birthDate.
  - value type is date.
  - value projection is age today at least 18 years.
